    "body": "Something to consider if this officially becomes opt-in via a `wheel` event. Many people didn't want this behavior and sought to avoid it. The suggested [fixes](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/9712295/disable-scrolling-on-input-type-number) [you](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/61480014/scrolling-on-a-type-number-input-to-change-its-value-how-to-stop-parents-scr) [find](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/63224459/disable-scrolling-on-input-type-number-in-react) [online](https://medium.com/modernnerd-code/how-to-disabled-scrolling-on-html-number-input-in-react-6548841166fb) generally consist of recommending something like this:\n\n```html\n<input type=\"number\" id=\"input\">\n<script>\n  input.addEventListener(\"wheel\", e => e.preventDefault())\n</script>\n```\n\nSo if this becomes conditional on the presence of a `wheel` event, the people who previously used `wheel` to _avoid_ the behavior would now be opting into that behavior instead.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
