    "body": "I wrote a series of test pages for this with various wheel event listeners. You can find it here: https://harmonious-quaint-cat.glitch.me/.\n\nBased on the behavior I'm seeing in Chromium, it seems that wheel event listeners are passive: false by default (vs passive: true like normal) when applied to a `input type=\"number\"` element. If you modify it to be `passive: true` then you get the undesirable behavior of a wheel both changing the value and scrolling the page. This applies even if the element with the passive listener is not the input element. I also found `e.preventDefault()` blocks the browser behavior of modifying the value. In all cases, unless the input element is focused and the mouse is over the input element, no value change happens.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
