    "created_at": "2026-05-29T21:39:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-29T21:39:03Z",
    "body": "I saw [Jake's](https://bsky.app/profile/jakearchibald.com/post/3mmt7ixfsek2v) [posts](https://mastodon.social/@jaffathecake/116645867765357032) about the bug in [Chromium 147–148](https://x.com/jaffathecake/status/2059644232671871456), and started playing with ways to get around it. First, I tried `preventDefault()` in a `wheel` event, and that stopped the mouse wheel from altering the input. But it also stopped scrolling of the page.\n\nThen, I noticed that the input value did not change when the input was hovered but not focused as the wheel scrolling started. So I tried blurring the input when a wheel event happens. Et voilà: wheel scrolls the page, and doesn't change the number input. (Not sure if there are any downsides to it.)\n\n```js\ndocument.addEventListener(\n  \"wheel\",\n  (e) => {\n    if (e.target.tagName === \"INPUT\" && e.target.type === \"number\") {\n      e.target.blur();\n    }\n  },\n  { passive: true },\n);\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
